Z||000000||snafus87||12-05-2001||10:25 PM||||ok...the last couple of days my battery light has been coming on really dim, BUT I haven't noticed any lights dimming under load or anything like that.  I went to AutoZone or AAP (can't remember which right now) and had them test the charging system...<P>Sure enough, my alternator anode pattern tested bad...<P>Anyway, my question:<P>How hard of a job (scale of 1 to 10) is changing the alternator in a V6?  I have ramps and such to lift the car and the tools, but are the ramps going to provide enough height to get under and get it out...OR can I pull it through the wheel well?<P>Just curious, as I'm not liking driving around like this and want to get it fixed ASAP<BR>(Would park it until time permitted to fix, but my wife-to-be wrecked our BMW and so she gets the AUTO lumina (can't drive stick too well)...<P>TIA<P>------------------<BR>JT Krupa<BR>85 GT<BR>(fastback conversion)<BR>180+ K miles<BR>Lehighton, PA||||reg||5
Z||000001||rogergarrison||12-05-2001||11:08 PM||||they say an  auto is harder than a manual. I have V6 4 spd. i just take out the little tube that blows on alt. jack up right rear. loosen belt tension bolt and belt. disconnect battery grnd.Remove alt pivot bolt from bracket. remove wires at alt. drop it out of bottom, takes a little bit of turning and manuevering. Takes me less than 30 mins.||||reg||1
Z||000002||NEPTUNE||12-06-2001||09:27 AM||||Its a litle more difficult with auto. It comes out thru the rr wheelwell, where the flex. splash shield is. You have to unbolt the control arm and push it out of the way. Be very careful not to damage the speed sensor, located just under the alt. ||||reg||6
Z||000003||carpetviper||12-06-2001||11:44 AM||||Yup I just got a new alt. for my '86 V6 about 3 weeks ago. Just suddenly died on me.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> Got a new one and it took about 30-45min w/ my dad and I to install.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/carpetviper.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by carpetviper (edited 12-06-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||snafus87||12-06-2001||05:07 PM||||Thanks for the info...<P>I have the Haynes manual AND the Factory Service Manual, but I just haven't been able to locate them since my move from Central PA to the Allentown area...<P>Probably will give it a try this weekend...doesn't sound all that hard...<P>Thanks again!||||reg||14
Z||000005||85 gt fiero||12-06-2001||08:55 PM||||just got done 5 minutes ago swapping alternators in my 85 gt 4spd took me 2 hours to do it probably would have gone by sooner if i hadnt have fallen asleep <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>RALLY CAR, FULL ROLL CAGE, SKID PLATES AND SOON TO BE BRIGHT YELLOW||||reg||1
